        {
          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"ddd2f5a8191c1ae70b57ec33\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"task_requirements\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Required: the No Service request calls for customer identification and applicable cellular-service troubleshooting before escalation. The setup includes several service blockers, including a SIM lock that cannot be fixed with a user tool.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0004\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"}],\"rationale\":\"Diagnosing the device and line requires distinguishing fixable blockers from the locked SIM, coordinating user-guided checks and fixes, and establishing when escalation is warranted. Setup actions themselves are not agent work.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":3}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_001\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Selected conditional endpoint: the completion design calls for transfer while service remains unavailable, and the SIM-security policy supports escalation once that blocker is established.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0314\"}],\"rationale\":\"The transfer call has a simple summary argument, but its use depends on prior diagnosis and the policy's restriction against premature transfer. It is not the entire troubleshooting workflow.\",\"applicability\":\"selected_conditional\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":2,\"tool_use\":1,\"information\":1}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Customer identification, device and line diagnosis, applicable corrective guidance, verification, and escalation form substantial multi-stage work; the initialization actions are excluded.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0206\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0218\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0222\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0027\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Several simultaneous causes must be distinguished. Billing suspension can be addressed under conditions, whereas a locked SIM calls for escalation; fixing one cause need not restore service.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0115\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The agent must select among customer, billing, line, and user-device checks, bind retrieved IDs to account actions where warranted, and use the transfer tool only after determining its condition is met.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0322\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0324\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0319\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0447\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0431\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Identification precedes support; payment and bill-status verification precede lifting an overdue-bill suspension, followed by reboot and service verification. User-guided diagnostics precede a justified handoff.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0106\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0115\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0117\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The agent must retrieve and reconcile device status with customer, line, and bill information; the user's No Service report alone does not identify which concurrent blockers remain.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0004\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0222\"}]}},\"overall_score\":75,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"A justified transfer to a human agent with the issue still in No Service status, rather than a claim that signal was restored.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"The documented escalation is conditional on trying applicable in-scope remedies and identifying the unfixable SIM-security issue. Billing and device remedies have their own ordered checks, but are not counted as independent alternative endpoints or as setup work.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Levels 3+3+3+3+3 yield 75. The difficulty lies in multi-cause diagnosis and coordinated, policy-constrained escalation, not in the single reference transfer call.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"The reference lists only the transfer, so the precise order and extent of preceding troubleshooting are not specified.\",\"The scenario names `get_status_bar`, while the supplied user tool and policy name `check_status_bar`; this naming mismatch does not prevent a source-based complexity assessment.\",\"The supplied sources do not establish observed tool results or actual completion.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"Reference action is an intended endpoint, not an execution trace or complete workflow.\",\"Baseline records precede initialization actions and are not facts supplied directly to the task agent.\",\"Scenario status-bar tool name differs from the supplied tool contract.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
